LOK: callbacks flush inline on every platform

0001 made the callback queue flush inline on macOS, where Aqua never
runs posted user events. Elsewhere scheduleFlush posted a user event,
so a callback reached the client only after the next turn of the
main loop. Ely's worker posts a command and waits for its result and
states inside the same request, which runs inside that loop (unipoll
on Linux, a window message on Windows): the result never came. The
queue now flushes inline everywhere; the flush event, its link and
stop() are gone.

